      "writtenOn": "2022-05-16T16:19:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Nit: this is actually not a valid value for any of the connectivity APIs that takes an argument annotated with @FirewallChain (setUidFirewallRule, setFirewallChainEnabled, replaceFirewallChain), right? If it isn\u0027t, we shouldn\u0027t add it to this @IntDef since that is used to document what the valid parameters are.\n\nMore in general: the fact that FIREWALL_CHAIN_LOCKDOWN_VPN cannot be passed to setUidFirewallRule, setFirewallChainEnabled, or replaceFirewallChain suggests that FIREWALL_CHAIN_LOCKDOWN_VPN isn\u0027t a firewall chain at all, but something different. The iif match isn\u0027t a firewall chain either.\n\nActually I think this constant is needed only because this CL uses BpfNetMaps#setUidRule to add and remove LOCKDOWN_VPN entries. I think we could delete it, see comment in TrafficController.cpp. But not necessary in this CL.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1003,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 1003,
        "endChar": 35
      },
      "revId": "b08654ca0450d021da709a762ab509a8d4f87d40",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
