      "message": "Nit: you might want to put the check for hasRestrictedNetworksPermission first, since it\u0027s simpler and might be faster (just a hashtable lookup instead of a linear scan of UID ranges). Something like:\n\n        // Apps that can use restricted networks can always bypass VPNs.\n        if (hasRestrictedNetworksPermission(uid)) {\n            return;\n        }\n\n        if (UidRange.containsUid(mVpnLockdownUidRanges.getSet(), uid) {\n            updateLockdownUidRule(uid, add);\n        }\n\nOn the other hand, it\u0027s true that app installs and uninstalls are mostly of non-privileged applications, so the hasRestrictedNetworksPermission check will mostly fail. So probably won\u0027t be much faster :-). Up to you.",
